meta {
  name: 01 Upload Document (pid1)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/documents
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: copilot_session={{copilot_session}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  patient_id: {{upload_patient_id}}
  doc_type: intake_form
  file: @file(/Users/taylorclements/Desktop/openemr-base-clean_clem/clinical-copilot/demo_documents/alice_intake_complete.png) @contentType(image/png)
}

docs {
  Auth: requires the copilot_session environment variable to be set to a
  real, still-valid session cookie -- see bruno/README.md's "Getting a
  session cookie into Bruno" section. Without it this 401s with
  {"detail": "Not logged in..."}.
  
  This is the one-shot ingestion entry point (app/main.py's POST
  /documents, PRD Section 4.2's attach_and_extract) -- runs real OCR + a
  real Anthropic structuring call once, at upload time. There is no
  in-page upload control anywhere in /ui (chat.html has no file input);
  this request is currently the only way to actually exercise this path
  outside a live demo click-through.
  
  Before running:
  1. Set the environment's upload_patient_id variable to whichever
     patient this upload is for (Alice: 98c4b82b-b07e-11f1-8334-
     022958ad0af8, Bob: 98c4c088-b07e-11f1-8334-022958ad0af8).
  2. doc_type must be exactly "lab_pdf" or "intake_form" -- edit the
     multipart body field above to match whichever you're uploading.
  3. Click the file field's value and browse to the real file on disk
     (Bruno's UI shows this as a file picker once you select the
     multipart-form body type; @file() in the raw .bru source is a
     placeholder Bruno fills in when you pick a file through that UI, not
     something you type by hand).
  
  Expect: 200 with the full ExtractionResult JSON (doc_id,
  extracted_doc_id, doc_type, extraction, ocr_avg_confidence) on success --
  read doc_id from the response if you need to reference this exact
  upload in a same-turn /chat call's uploaded_document_ref. A 409 means
  this exact file's content was already uploaded for this patient
  (store_extraction's content-hash idempotency check, not an error to
  work around) -- upload a genuinely different file, or just move on to
  /chat if the point was confirming the upload worked at all.
}
